    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nOpening a Telescope window while the mini.files file explorer is opened closes both windows. However, opening the file explorer when the Telescope window is opened behaves as expected - closing the Telescope window and opening the file explorer.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.11.0-nightly+82b02ae\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n1. Press `<space>fm` to open the mini.files file explorer.\r\n1. Press `<space>/` to open the Telescope window\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n---@diagnostic disable: undefined-global\r\n-- DO NOT change the paths and don't remove the colorscheme\r\nvim.g.mapleader = \" \"\r\nvim.g.maplocalleader = \" \"\r\nlocal root = vim.fn.fnamemodify(\"./.repro\", \":p\")\r\n\r\n-- set stdpaths to use .repro\r\nfor _, name in ipairs({ \"config\", \"data\", \"state\", \"cache\" }) do\r\n  vim.env[(\"XDG_%s_HOME\"):format(name:upper())] = root .. \"/\" .. name\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- bootstrap lazy\r\nlocal lazypath = root .. \"/plugins/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n  vim.fn.system({ \"git\", \"clone\", \"--filter=blob:none\", \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\", lazypath })\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.runtimepath:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\n-- install plugins\r\nlocal plugins = {\r\n  {\r\n    \"echasnovski/mini.files\",\r\n    version = \"*\",\r\n    keys = {\r\n      {\r\n        \"<leader>fm\",\r\n        function()\r\n          require(\"mini.files\").open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0), true)\r\n        end,\r\n        desc = \"Open mini.files (Directory of Current File)\",\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim\",\r\n    keys = function()\r\n      local builtin = require(\"telescope.builtin\")\r\n      return {\r\n        {\r\n          \"<leader>/\",\r\n          function()\r\n            builtin.live_grep({})\r\n          end,\r\n          desc = \"Live grep\",\r\n        },\r\n      }\r\n    end,\r\n    dependencies = { \"nvim-lua/plenary.nvim\" },\r\n  },\r\n}\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup(plugins, {\r\n  root = root .. \"/plugins\",\r\n})\r\n\r\n```\r\n![demo](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0c44a04a-6154-4f82-8b24-f6e7a6ecf3c3)\r\n\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe file explorer should stay opened, when the Telescope window is opened.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nBoth windows disappear after a significant delay.",
