            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThis is an expected behavior. The reason for this is to detect whether the user left the explorer windows (accidentally, or via mouse) and autoclose explorer. Opening a Telescope window is treated in the same way: as it is not a 'mini.files' buffer, explorer is closed (via `MiniFiles.close()`) and focus is returned to its original target window.\r\n\r\nCouple of extra notes:\r\n- It is recommended to first close an explorer and only then use any other functionality which changes buffer/window.\r\n- There is no such problem with 'mini.pick' :)\r\n\r\nClosing as working as expected.",
